# Copy to .env.local and adjust. Unset defaults to Solana Devnet, where the
# program is deployed live (phase 8.2). The wallet-adapter cluster is
# derived from the endpoint automatically.
#
# Dedicated devnet RPC is strongly recommended: the public
# api.devnet.solana.com endpoint 429-storms under the app's poll load
# (2026-10-07 incident). Placeholder only — NEVER commit a real API key;
# real values live in .env.local (gitignored).
# VITE_SOLANA_RPC_URL=https://devnet.helius-rpc.com/?api-key=YOUR_HELIUS_DEVNET_KEY

# Which ORB deployment the game talks to (SDK program id + PDAs). Unset =
# devnet. Production sets VITE_ORB_CLUSTER=mainnet together with a mainnet
# VITE_SOLANA_RPC_URL at launch (docs/runbooks/mainnet-launch.md phase 7).
# VITE_ORB_CLUSTER=mainnet
#
# Local validator (the phase 7.5 demo runbook):
# VITE_SOLANA_RPC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8899
VITE_SOLANA_RPC_URL=https://api.devnet.solana.com

# ── ORE Lite (/ore-lite — mainnet feature, see
#    apps/web/src/features/ore-lite/README.md) ────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED for /ore-lite: the platform-fee treasury wallet (base58). The
# feature intentionally fails loudly at load when unset — a missing fee
# must never ship silently. The main app at / is unaffected either way.
# VITE_ORE_FEE_RECIPIENT=YourTreasuryWalletBase58Here
#
# Strongly recommended: a dedicated mainnet RPC (Helius, Triton, QuickNode,
# Alchemy). The public api.mainnet-beta endpoint 403s browser origins, so
# the page renders its error state without this.
# VITE_ORE_RPC_URL=https://your-mainnet-rpc-endpoint/your-api-key
#
# Auto-join (multi-round Automate) — the no-keeper design uses ORE's
# permissionless executor; there is no keeper key. Any truthy value turns
# the ROUNDS control on. Leave unset until the P5 dust run has validated
# our setup/stop combo (the bot-fleet execution path is already
# live-proven).
# VITE_ORE_AUTOJOIN_ENABLED=1
